      "name": "Adyen active incident: Degraded performance for in-person payments on a subset of Android devices August 05 2026, 14:42 CEST Payments Updated August 05 2026, 15:02 CEST As of 14:52 CEST on August 5, 2026, we have implemented mitigation measures for the issue affecting Android Tap to Pay on devices with Rockchip processors, first identified at 14:05 CEST. Following these measures, we are seeing a decrease in transaction failures caused by attestation errors. Our engineering teams continue to monitor the situation closely and are working towards a full resolution. We will share a further update as soon as it becomes available. Identified August 05 2026, 14:42 CEST We have identified an externally caused issue that started at 14:05 CEST on August 5, 2026, affecting Android Tap to Pay on devices with Rockchip processors. This issue is resulting in failures during attestation, which in turn cause transaction failures. As a result, affected devices are unable to process Tap to Pay transactions. Our engineering teams are actively investigating and implementing mitigation measures to restore service. We will share a further update as soon as it becomes available. Payout delay for a subset of BRL transactions August 03 2026, 15:22 CEST Settlement and payouts",
